      "body": "Closing as **methodology recorded, applies to a future #531 run** (this is a pre-registration note for when #531's compute-bound past-knee runs happen, not a standalone change).\n\nRecorded for the next #531 β-pinning pass: (1) windowed exponent fits — report restricted-window AND full-range β, don't collapse to one; (2) a permuted/null exponent arm so saturation reads as ratio-vs-null rather than absolute-law failure; (3) a pre-registered Δβ drift threshold (historical program used Δα ≤ 0.10). Basis: the historical routing-capacity law steepened α 0.572→0.657 over K=600–5000 while the null grew faster (ratio stable 2.6–2.8×); a single global exponent underestimated by up to +65% at K=5000. Reopen/apply when #531 executes past-knee.",
